description:
Fixes #25.

Replace derived comparison traits on `ActorId` with manual implementations that route through `to_bytes()` marked `#[inline(never)]`:

   ```rust
   #[derive(Hash, Clone)]
   pub struct ActorId(TinyVec<[u8; 16]>);

   impl PartialEq for ActorId {
       fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {
           self.to_bytes() == other.to_bytes()
       }
   }
   impl Eq for ActorId {}
   impl PartialOrd for ActorId {
       fn partial_cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Option<Ordering> {
           Some(self.cmp(other))
       }
   }
   impl Ord for ActorId {
       fn cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Ordering {
           self.to_bytes().cmp(other.to_bytes())
       }
   }
   ```

   ```rust
   #[inline(never)]
   pub fn to_bytes(&self) -> &[u8] {
       &self.0
   }
   ```

The `#[inline(never)]` barrier ensures callers only see a fully-initialised `&[u8]` fat pointer, preventing the compiler from inlining through to the raw `ArrayVec` backing array. Comparison semantics (lexicographic byte ordering) are preserved. 

Performance impact is negligible — `ActorId` comparisons are not on a hot path, and `migrate_actors` is explicitly documented as "an uncommon operation."
